issions checked. Refusals have context and frozen turns cannot be rewritten.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-006: Duplicate/unknown requirement references, context limits and workspace isolation checked; unresolved references are explicit instead of invented.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007: Crash before/after claim/start, lease renewal/takeover, repeated sweep candidates and newer-run completion checked. Duplicate expiry fails R3-F01.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008: Single line then silence, long runtime, reviewer-root exit with descendants, cancellation before heartbeat/at Close and owner death checked. Streaming and no deadline pass; refused Fail continuation fails R3-F05.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-009: Permanent corrupt payload, nonretryable append conflict, server-versus-reviewer attribution, shutdown excluded from counted attempts and failed triage dispatch checked. Bounds are explicit; outcome propagation fails R3-F05.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-010: Missing/duplicate/malformed records, extra/missing turn assessment, score-only DISAGREE, a response closed before verification and before commit checked. Immutable admitted-set predicate resolves round 2 race.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-011: Each Request/log/result write and each public/internal decompression read, missing/reordered chunk, round-trip mismatch and persistent codec failure checked. Bounded result/brief server-fault handling passes; wire propagation fails R3-F06 and replay omission R3-F03.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-012: Crash at verification/transaction/outbox, concurrent successful finalizers, late Fail, cancel-at-close and old Finalizing request checked. Finalizer atomicity and own Fail guards pass; sweep can revive terminal state R3-F01.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-013: Reviewer self/session/family independence, submitted self-review preservation and threshold binding checked; explicit finalization origin is distinct from self-review.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-014: AGREE and DISAGREE finalization do not set TODO/requirement done states; notifications carry verdict only.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-015: Not-ready, absent, removed and corrupt result/evidence, original gzip versus decompressed download and full current-run projection checked. Last-output sequence and replay gaps R3-F03/F06.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-016: Reconnect cursor, new attempt, duplicate delivery, quiet producer, malformed cursor, removed output and corrupt chunk checked. Stream event fields disagree R3-F06.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-017: Outbox commit versus wake-up, watcher crash before/after inbox/cursor, submit completing after notification, request versus author scope and unsupported host checked. Atomic local inbox and prompt-delivery boundary preserve at-least-once behavior.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018: Every mutation and all evidence consumers, ledger unavailable before read, rollback after read and replay with output checked. Write hard stop passes; probe and Submit audit gaps R3-F02/F03.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-019: Active-request removal refusal, repeated explicit removal, subsequent read/replay and audit-history preservation checked; no automatic payload or ledger purge is authorized.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-020: REST/MCP/client/REPL/Director/plugin aliases, caller origin, unsupported-host inert behavior, cross-workspace dispatch and complete response coverage checked. Exact stream/sequence parity fails R3-F06.
- FR-MCP-HVPIPE-021: Mode Off, Closed/superseded/rejected responses, duplicate grade, atomic completion, retained findings after removal and self-grading exclusion checked. Closed-result persistence fixes pass; nonretryable grade-conflict caller is incomplete R3-F05.

Evidence limits and rejected false positives: these are design-level counterexamples, not claims that nonexistent HV implementation was executed. Future H1 qualification and live checks remain future gates, not UNKNOWN results for work claimed completed. The Cline failed-provider debug log contains a requested reasoning_effort value; this is not proof of effective effort of a successful run, so it does not overturn D-06. Record-read timestamps generated by RequirementsWorkflow are not evidence of D-09 edits. Foundation ReadableKeyAllocator already truncates long parent keys deterministically, so the child-id length concern was rejected. The .NET GZIP experiment does not prove storage cost; the amendment correctly leaves that measurement open. Earlier implementer conduct and unrelated foundation/federation work were not scored.

Reviewer process disclosures: some initial and diagnostic read/check commands were inline PowerShell rather than checked .ps1 files; no Python, Node, bash script or powershell.exe was used. One Render WhatIf was run after an analyzer warning about the automatic Matches variable; it made no write, the variable was corrected and the script was re-parsed and analyzed with zero findings before the actual receipt write. Early tool wrappers displayed text without retaining every outer-shell exit code; those command-audit entries retain an empty ExitCodes array, not an invented zero. Native git/gh/CLI/plugin exit codes are independently recorded. Known command failures were a no-match rg and the rejected initial session open, both preserved and corrected. These are my deviations, not implementer findings. Written scripts were parser/analyzer checked, with any initial diagnostic findings corrected; state-writing receipt scripts were dry-run. No product build/test was appropriate under this review-only code freeze.

